# Security Policy

## Supported versions

The latest release is supported. Before the first tagged release, the current
`main` branch is supported.

## Reporting a vulnerability

Do not disclose suspected vulnerabilities in a public issue, discussion, pull
request, or chat transcript.

[% if github_owner %]
Use [GitHub private vulnerability reporting](https://github.com/[[ github_owner | trim | regex_replace('^@', '') ]]/[[ project_slug ]]/security/advisories/new).
[% else %]
Use GitHub private vulnerability reporting when it is enabled for this
repository. Otherwise, ask a maintainer for a private reporting channel without
including sensitive details publicly.
[% endif %]

Include the affected version, security impact, minimal reproduction steps, and
any known mitigation. Remove credentials, personal data, and unrelated system
information from the report.

Allow maintainers time to reproduce, assess, fix, and release a correction
before public disclosure.
